  "narrative": {
    "intro": "W S Darley and obligated $1B in FY2026 to date across 1,981 federal awards. The company recorded an average award size of $522K. Obligations fell 30.4% year over year. Fiscal-year trends show rising obligations from FY21 through FY25, peaking at $1.5B in FY25 before the current-year drop to $1B. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, accounting for $1B of obligations in FY2026 to date, while the General Services Administration and the Department of Justice are distant second and third with $4M and $2M respectively. Market activity clusters in two NAICS groups: Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers with $544M, and All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing with $450M. Smaller markets include Photographic and Photocopying Equipment Manufacturing at $13.9M and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing at $11.1M. The totals reported are contract obligations, except for award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity.",
